# No GCC asm labels in decompiled C

`register T x asm("rN")` and empty `asm("")` barriers are banned in semantic C.
They pin registers / instruction order and are not a real match.

Allowed `asm()`:

- BIOS: `asm("swi N");`
- Naked readable Thumb / opcode stubs (`__attribute__((naked))`)

If agbcc will not emit retail bytes without an asm label, park the C (`park_wip.py`) and leave Thumb in `src/matched/`.
